## Notes for the Architect

1. **Behaviour change in M5 rollback:** after a refused link, the shell now keeps the advanced link pair, so the refused request isn't read and answered again. Without this, a failed DHT require would restart a load of the failed address. All existing tests pass.
2. **Head-of-line waiting (existing behaviour, unchanged):** a require abandoned while its closure is still loading stays first in the request queue. A later require on the same session waits behind it until that load finishes or fails.
3. **No diagnostics on an unknown name yet:** in L3 the refusal for an unresolved name is just `{:reason :absent :name n}`. Diagnostics come with principals in L4.
4. **What "raised data" means here:** the cross-host check compares the refusal map the interpreter writes back to the require. The engine raises that same map (plus `:link-module`) as the error data; the shell itself only shows the error as text.
